  "justification": "All core genome-scale quantities reported by Blattner et al.—genome size, GC content, CDS count, mean CDS length, coding density, tRNA and rRNA counts, and gene co-orientation with replication—match the NC_000913.3 measurements within small, expected deltas attributable to curation and annotation refinement. Differences are minor (e.g., +0.052% length, ~1.7 percentage-point lower coding density, +0.7% CDS count) and consistent with post-1997 error correction and community updates. Metrics not explicitly claimed in the 1997 paper (start-codon breakdown and per-base composition) were not included in scoring."
